 This install applies to "Red Baron" © 1992 Sierra/Dynamix.

 This install requires WHDLoad 17 or later to be in the path. It can be found in the
 WHDLoad package.

 The tested minimum is 0.5 MB ChipMem and 2 MB FastMem.
 It can be quit by pressing num '*' (key can be changed with Tooltype "QuitKey=").

 The game requires an installed A500 Kickstart 1.3 image.
 The kickstart image must be located in the directory "Devs:Kickstarts" and
 must be named "kick34005.A500". The image can be extracted from a A500 with
 tools like 'GrabKick' or similar which can be found on aminet.
 If the image is of wrong version or altered in any way WHDLoad will quit with
 an appropriate requester.
 Additionally the file "kick34005.A500.RTB" must be installed in the same
 directory as the kickstart image. It can be found in the archive 
 "util/boot/skick346.lha" on aminet.

 If you have problems with this installation please try and get a newer
 version of this package from the WHDLoad WWW-Page. If that doesn't help try
 some Tooltypes like NOCACHE, NOAUTOVEC, NOVBRMOVE, NOMMU, PAL or NTSC. If
 that also fails, please inform the author via the Bug-Report-Form which
 can be accessed on the WHDLoad WWW-Page or create a mantis issue directly
 at http://mantis.whdload.de

 For the full WHDLoad package, other installs and updates refer to:
	http://www.whdload.de/
 or	aminet:dev/misc/whdload#?
 and	aminet:game/patch/

 The slave reserves 1 MB for game and renderer memory, plus Kickstart.
 The former 512 KB ChipMem + 1.5 MB slow-RAM configuration is insufficient.
 Tested minimum: 512 KB ChipMem + 2 MB FastMem (normal-build flight).
 Faster rendering releases the 192 KB game-pool extension for sim v1.
 With the option off, the game retains its original allocation budget.
 DMA allocations retain their original ChipMem requests.
 Faster rendering enables instruction caching on 020+ where needed.
 It does not enable a disabled data cache. On a 68030 with an MMU, use
 the MMU tooltype to permit fast-memory data caching; ChipMem stays uncached.
 Current maximum-detail measurements show less than 2% difference with MMU,
 below the resolution of the FPS window; no speedup is claimed for the tooltype.

 Rendering improvements:
 - Faster rendering is On by default (normal build: CUSTOM2=0). It selects the verified dashboard cache, geometry,
   solid-fill, persistent-gauge and sound optimizations, with CPU-specific choices.
 - Persistent gauge reuse is enabled only on the measured 020/040 classes.
 - Flight swaps use the original safe beam wait and a two-field cap (about
   25 FPS on PAL). This does not make world speed frame-rate independent.
 - Select Off in the splash window, or CUSTOM2=1, to disable it.
   This reverses the former development normal-build 0/1 meaning.
   Supplied icon tooltypes are unchanged.
 - Applies only to sim v1; v2/v3 retain their existing fixes.
 - The dashboard cache uses about 13.7 KB extra ChipMem, with allocation fallback.
 - Faster frames can accelerate the world on slow machines. Time Scale remains
   unchanged; consistent-speed acceptance is postponed.
 - Developer builds retain individual CUSTOM2 bits (CUSTOM2=0 disables all).
   Their bit-13 consistent-speed candidate is not enabled in this release.
   Normal/developer builds
   contain no VERIFY instruments or scripted game input.

 Performance and Time Scale:
 - The current release accepts measured performance, without a 50 FPS claim.
   The profiling scoreboard records the six machine configurations; the final
   normal-build refresh is pending the release checks.
 - The normal build retains the original frame-dependent game speed on all
   CPUs. No frame-independent Time Scale envelope is claimed for this release.
 - Developer candidate only: A500 Time Scale 0 passed the rate window;
   maximum-detail Time Scale 40 dropped simulation time. 020/030/040/060
   passed their Time Scale 40 rate windows. These are not full gameplay
   acceptance or normal-build guarantees. Reduce detail on slower machines.

